# Open-SWE long-8 (2026-10-30): the 8 longest sessions of the draw uncut (prompts to 254,024): 4 streams with a 262,144-token
# window each (~5.2 GiB per stream, ~21 GiB), the rest of the pool for kept prompts; agents past 4 wait in the queue.
# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: the recipe's default checkpoint, NVIDIA's FP4-Local (the same one vLLM's eugr recipe serves)
MODEL_REPO=nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local
MODEL_REVISION=b9ce18a6887e18c089fdea8509a33e63429a3300   # the recipe's pin (scripts/config.sh)
# The comparison's setting, inside the 102 GiB budget. The recipe serves 5 requests with a 262,144-token window each.
# TensorFold 1.1.4 gives every stream a full window at start and keeps prompts in what is left of its pool: so 16
# streams (the most the recipe's start.sh takes), each with a window the suite's largest requests fit in, the rest of
# the pool for kept prompts. Text only: VISION=0 gives the vision helper's 2 GiB back to the pool. Nothing else changes.
# The window is 40,960, not the 36,864 the largest request needs: the recipe's patch 0005 gives a stream's MTP head a
# bf16 cache unless the stream comes within a twentieth of the window, then fp8, and a kept state restores only into the
# same head format. At 36,864, a 32k prompt primed with 1 token (bf16 head) and timed with 1,024 (fp8 head) was refused
# its restore (RestoreRejected) and prefilled again (restore_probe.py, 2026-10-28). 8k and 16k ran at 36,864 (no
# request near the line there).
PARALLEL=4
TF_CONTEXT=${TF_CONTEXT:-262144}
VISION=0
SETTING_DESC="recipe defaults (fp8 KV, MTP drafts, thinking on) with PARALLEL $PARALLEL, CONTEXT $TF_CONTEXT, VISION 0 (recipe: 5, 262144, 1); pool = MemAvailable at start less ENGINE_BUDGET_GIB"
ENGINE_LABEL="TensorFold $TF_VERSION (${TF_REF:0:8} + recipe patches 0001-0017), MiaAI-Lab recipe ${RECIPE_COMMIT:0:7}, image $TF_IMAGE, ${MODEL_REPO}@${MODEL_REVISION:0:7}"
